        "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{-4+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{8}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
